.TH RAKC 1 "2026-09-10" "rakc 0.5.0" "Rak compiler"
.SH NAME
rakc \- compiler and interpreter for the Rak programming language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rakc
.I <command>
.RI [ <file> ]
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run <file>
Run a Rak script on the tree-walking interpreter.
.TP
.B vm <file>
Run on the bytecode VM (~6x faster).
.TP
.B build <file>
Build a standalone executable with the source embedded.
.TP
.B bench <file>
Benchmark interpreter vs VM.
.TP
.B check <file>
Lex and parse, print diagnostics with line/column.
.TP
.B lex <file>
Print tokens.
.TP
.B parse <file>
Print the AST.
.TP
.B repl
Start an interactive REPL.
.TP
.B lsp
Start the language server (stdio).
.TP
.B bindgen <h>
Generate Rak bindings from a C header.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RAK_PATH
Search path for \fBimport\fR name-based module resolution (\fB;\fR on Windows,
\fB:\fR on Unix).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run a script:
.B rakc run examples/hello.rak
.PP
Build a standalone binary:
.B rakc build examples/hello.rak
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rakpkg (1)
